we just got some major bombshell leaks  for the iphone 14 pro which include both  good and bad news but i think the good  news is so good that the bad news isn't  even gonna matter at this point so  without further ado i'm gonna get into  the bad news about the iphone 14 pro  first and then i'll get into the crazy  leaks about the new camera system and  why it's gonna be the biggest camera  update we've ever had you've probably  been seeing these leaked renders  floating around the internet over the  past week or so showing off a new iphone  design that features the dual hole punch  camera cut out on the front display  which i think is extremely exciting and  i personally think it's going to look  amazing in person but when you go over  to the back side the camera bump looks  almost identical to the one we already  have on the iphone 13 pro so when i  first saw these renders i thought they  were fake but we just got some  confirmation from the most important  source in regards to the iphone 14  design yes that's john prosser because  back in september right before the  iphone 13 design reveal he decided to  leak the iphone 14 design which he said  would have a completely flush glass back  as well as a single hole punch camera on  the front and obviously that was very  exciting because that design would be  completely unique since it would get rid  of the squares camera bump on the back  that we currently have but to be honest  right from the start i had my doubts  about this design and the reason for  that is because we've had some very  specific camera leaks from ming chi quo  claiming that the iphone 14 pro would  come with a 48 megapixel camera capable  of shooting 8k video so to me it seemed  absolutely impossible for apple to  somehow pull off completely flush  cameras on the back of the new iphone  design so because of that i worked with  renders by shylesh to create some iphone  14 pro renders based on john prosser's  renders created by ian zelbo but with my  own predictions added to it and the main  difference i added was having the flush  glass back but actually protruding the  three main camera bumps further out from  the frame because to me there's no way  they could have flush camera design if  they're upgrading to a new 48 megapixel  camera so it's gonna have to stick out  and with that said guess what just  happened the other day john prosser  himself made a new video admitting that  his flush iphone 14 pro design might  actually be for the iphone 15 instead so  it's very likely that his leaks were  just very early and he even said that  these recent leaked renders are probably  the actual new iphone 14 pro design so  basically we now have various sources  agreeing that the rear squarish camera  bump design will likely be sticking  around for another year and that right  there is the bad news because we've all  been hyped up for a complete iphone  redesign but it looks like we're only  getting a partial redesign this time  with the removal of the notch on the  display but don't worry because like i  said in the intro i believe that the  good news that was just leaked far  outweighs the bad news so let's get  right into it way back in april of 2021  almost a full year ago ming chu ko  reported that the new high-end 2022  iphone 14 pro models would come with a  48 megapixel camera that is capable of  shooting 8k video and making it even  better he said that the new camera would  be capable of supporting both 48  megapixel output while simultaneously 48  megapixel output while simultaneously  outputting 12 megapixel photos by  utilizing pixel binning to essentially  merge four nearby pixels into one larger  pixel which significantly increases the  pixel size up to about 2.5 microns which  is larger than any android phone out  there so makes you close predictions  back in april of last year were that  this new 48 megapixel sensor would  elevate mobile phone camera photography  to a new level and i completely agree  but now almost a full year later we've  gotten multiple reports that back up  what ming has been saying all along  including a report from trend force  claiming that the 48 megapixel camera is  coming to the iphone 14 pro models and  just the other day ming chakra tweeted  in agreement about the new leaked iphone  14 pro schematics claiming that the new  larger and more prominent rear camera of  the 14 pro models is due to apple  upgrading the wide camera to 48  megapixels and then to put the cherry on  top we just got a bombshell leak from a  weibo account detailing the actual specs  and features of the iphone 14 pro's new  48 megapixel camera and as you can see  there are a bunch of confusing bits of  info with no explanation but luckily we  here at maxtec used to actually review  cameras and compare them and we used to  shoot weddings full time so we know a  thing or two about cameras so let's go  ahead and dig into each little detail  starting with the one slash 1.3 inches  which is actually the sensor size which  is going to be similar to the one to the  s22 ultra around  69.12 millimeters squared and if you  want to compare that to the current  iphone 13 pro max's main camera sensor  it's actually going to be 57  larger than the current one which is a  huge difference  now moving on to the next detail we have  1.22 um dpaf  and dpaf means dual pixel autofocus  which is currently the standard now 1.22  um stands for 1.22 microns which is a  measure of the size of each individual  pixel and on the surface it looks like a  downgrade compared to the pixel size of  the current iphone 13 pro which is  sitting at 1.9 microns but before you  think this is really bad news the reason  for the smaller pixel size is because  there are now four times as many pixels  inside of the sensor since we're going  from a 12 megapixel sensor to a 48  megapixel so the pixels themselves have  to get smaller and the pixel size  directly impacts how much light enters  into each pixel so a smaller 1.22 micron  pixel size means less light entering the  pixel which means worse low light  performance because apple's gonna have  to raise the iso or the artificial  exposure to properly adjust the  brightness for a dim or low light  scenario but wait a minute since apple  is gonna be utilizing pixel bidding to  merge four pixels together into one thus  outputting a 12 megapixel photo from  that 48 megapixel sensor the effective  pixel size actually gets doubled from  1.22 microns up to  2.44 microns which is almost exactly  what ming chico reported last year in  april and this new 2.44 micron pixel  size is gonna be a huge deal because  it's actually gonna let  28.4 percent more light come into the  sensor compared to the iphone 13 pro  sensor with 1.9 micron pixels which is  going to be a very big deal for low  light photography and videography but  the main problem with all of this is  that larger sensors like the 57 larger  one going into the iphone 14 pro  actually require longer and larger glass  elements that protrude even more in  order to maintain the same aperture so  if apple were to maintain the same f 1.5  aperture on this new much larger sensor  the camera bump would have to stick out  quite a bit more than it already is and  the crazy thing that backs that up is  that main chaquelle came out with a  report saying that the diagonal length  of the 48 megapixel camera will increase  by 25 to 35  while the height of the seven layer lens  will increase by five to ten percent  which is why the new leaked renders are  showing a much larger camera bump that  protrudes even more than the current  iphone 13 pro now with that out of the  way let's move on to the next detail in  the list dual 11  12 bit ad which relates to the sensor  shooting 11 or 12 bit colors and then  converting it down to 8 or 10 bit that  apple uses and right below that the  pixel level bonding and dram on the chip  will be used for hardware level pixel  binning of taking the 48 megapixel  sensor and converting it into a 12  megapixel photo or video recording and i  do want to mention that when it's very  bright outside the camera will likely  automatically use the full 48 megapixel  sensor for maximum detail but when it  starts to get dim or even in dark low  light the camera will automatically  switch to binning down to 12 megapixels  to take advantage of the larger 2.44  micron pixel size when bini now moving  on to the next detail we have clear hdr  which i believe stands for apple's  extended dynamic range video recording  which combines two different exposures  to get better hdr results and then dol  hdr stands for dolby vision hdr and the  dol clear hdr stands for dolby vision  recording while also using the extended  dynamic range now below that i honestly  don't know what these two things mean so  i won't even try but moving further we  have various recording formats using the  full resolution sensor but that does not  matter because apple always shoots video  in 16x9 format which is actually at the  bottom of the list the first 16x9 12-bit  120fps option means that the sensor is  actually capable of recording 8k  resolution at 120fps which i don't think  apple will even allow and below that we  have clear hdr at 60 fps so that's 8k  60fps with extended dynamic range  enabled which is gonna be the absolute  game changer and then finally dolby  vision extended dynamic range with  11-bit colors at 24 fps which will be  the flagship 8k format so basically with  all of that said and explained the point  that i'm trying to make is that the  iphone 14 pro models will get a massive  step up in terms of camera quality  destroying the other android phones that  currently already shoot 8k video but  they're limited to only 24 fps and the  quality is sometimes even worse than the  iphone's current 4k video quality so if  you're thinking about buying an iphone  13 pro right now i would honestly hold  off until the iphone 14 pro models are  revealed because i think this will be by  far the biggest camera update we've ever  seen on the iphone and with that said  hopefully you enjoyed this video and if  you did go ahead and click the circle  above to subscribe for more videos like  this one and definitely check out one of  those two right over there thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  video  [Music]

